                  </origin>
                  <provenance type="#e" source="3029"><orgName role="fmo" key="mlgbOrg_245">Haughmond, Shropshire.
                        Augustinian abbey of St John the Evangelist</orgName><p>"Anno domini
                        millesimo [sic; add: quingentesimo] tricesimo septimo Thomas Abbas
                        acquisiuit istum librum huic monasterio. qui aliquando fuit prioratus de
                        Ronton vicelicet ante suppressionem eiusdem que eadem [sic] anno factus
                        [sic] est per actum parliamenti" (fol. 157r, at foot). Above this is written
                        "haghmond". </p></provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">"Roberte Parkar owe this boke" (fol. 1r), s.
                     xvi.</provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">"per me Johannem Sewell" (fol.
                     156r).</provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">"Thomas Mawnsell" (fol. 1r).</provenance>
               <provenance type="#e" source="4491"><orgName role="fmo" key="mlgbOrg_457">Ranton, Staffordshire.
                        Augustinian priory of St Mary the Virgin</orgName><p>'... aliquando fuit
                        prioratus de Ronton ...' (see further under Haughmond).</p><p>The use seems
                        to be Augustinian.</p></provenance>
